<section class="section blush">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How I teach pitching</span>
      <h2>Seven steps from confusing to compelling</h2>
      <p>The framework from my masterclasses. Most bad pitches aren't bad ideas. They're unclear communication.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><h3>Hook</h3><p>Start with curiosity. Not your name, not your business name.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Problem</h3><p>Make the pain relatable. That's your tension.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Shift</h3><p>The "what if there was another way" moment.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Solution</h3><p>One sentence, no jargon, easy to repeat.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Proof</h3><p>People don't believe ideas. They believe evidence.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Ask</h3><p>Say exactly what you want from the room.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Pressure test</h3><p>Numbers, competitors, why now. Be ready for the questions.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="test">
      <span class="script">The test:</span>
      <span>If I grabbed someone outside the room, could they explain your pitch back to me?</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

